    "content": {
      "component": "blog_article",
      "sharepoint_id": "93",
      "title": "From Frustration to Transformation",
      "description": "A Nurse's Journey to Mental Well-Being",
      "date": "Nov 05, 2025",
      "read_time": "3 min read",
      "author": "Maureen Ooko",
      "isGlobal": true,
      "banner_image": {
        "fieldtype": "asset",
        "_local": "93-Banner.png"
      },
      "thumbnail": {
        "fieldtype": "asset"
      },
      "languages": [],
      "show_share": true,
      "show_similar": true,
      "similar_show_header": true,
      "category": "",
      "isFeatured": null,
      "body": [
        {
          "component": "rich_text",
          "content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mercy, not her real name, a Nurse in-charge and Director at a Medical Centre in Nairobi, recalls the frustration she would feel while on duty."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"As I went about my supervisory duties, I would follow up with patients after their sessions to understand if they received appropriate care and guidance. Sometimes I would discover that the patients were not well taken care of, despite the team having all the information they needed. It was upsetting.\""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Situations such as these would aggravate Mercy. At times, she admits, she felt like lashing out at her staff, wondering why they ignored clear instructions that could improve patients' health outcomes."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A new way of leading",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The turning point for Mercy came after she and her colleagues enrolled in the Mental Well-being and Resilience Programme offered by the Aga Khan University Institute for Human Development. The programme, supported by the Johnson & Johnson Foundation, was designed to help health care workers improve their mental well-being."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "One incident stands out clearly in Mercy's memory. As she spoke to mothers visiting the clinic, she realised that they were not receiving all the necessary reproductive health information. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"I reached out to the nurse responsible and asked her to counsel the mothers before they left the clinic,\" Mercy says. A few days later, I found out it was still not happening. \"Before the training, I might have confronted her angrily. However, this time, I took some time to calm down and then walked over to her station to talk to her.''"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The nurse explained that the task was new to her routine, so she sometimes forgot to incorporate it but promised to improve."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mercy realised that by staying calm and seeking to understand first, she could resolve problems without creating tension.  "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"My response to difficult situations has changed,\" she says. \"Now I take time to analyse the problem, manage my emotions, and act in a way that actually helps.\""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Her new leadership style, coupled with the mental health literacy training that her staff went through, led to a positive transformation in the health centre."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"The team became more cooperative, more open, and more motivated to do things right,\" Mercy adds."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Personal growth",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The benefits of the training extended far beyond her workplace. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Before, Mercy often harboured stress which affected her personal relationships. \"I would constantly worry about things that were out of my control. As a result, I became moody and sometimes this led to conflicts with my family.\""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Through the training, Mercy learned practical tools for coping with anxiety and managing her emotions."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"I now acknowledge when I am feeling overwhelmed and give myself time to cool down,\" she explains. \"I focus on the things I can change instead of worrying about what I cannot.\""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "This mindset shift has brought more peace into her personal life. \"I prioritise positive actions for my family during difficult times,\" Mercy says. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "For Mercy, the Mental Health Literacy training was not just about learning new skills. It was about transforming how she sees herself, her work and the people around her."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mercy is among the 600 health care workers who went through the transformative training that took place over an eight-week period in various health facilities in Nairobi."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
